Dear Governor Jeb Bush;
About nine (9) years ago a family by the name of SCHURICK moved into 419 =
Allspice Court here in Poinciana, Kissimmee, Florida because of health =
problems.

They brought along their mother (Mary's mom) because she had Alzheimer's =
Disease and could not take care of herself.  In time Mary's mom died.

This family of four purchased this beautiful home so they could finally =
live comfortably in their senior years.  This house being their final =
large purchase was a joy for all !!!

As life would have it, Bill's mother came down with Alzheimer's Disease =
and again, willingly they took her in until this day, caring for her.

August 13th, Friday of 2004 came Hurricane Charlie along with three =
tornados!  A horrible time came to Poinciana and nearly left us all in =
chaos.

Although the SCHURICK'S had much roof destroyed, they all went =
door-to-door to see if anyone needed help.  No one had electricity, all =
scrambling around.  What to do??  With fright on our faces.  Truly the =
SCHURICK'S with no experience of storms of this magnitude were there.

A knock came on our door, Bill, Mary and son Louis going from house to =
house to see what they could do for their neighbors and then some.

Daily was their endeavor to care for others first, what was needed =
mostly was water and ice as we all had no refrigeration.  The SCHURICK'S =
traveled in their vehicles over ninety (90) miles, at times one way to =
pick up bags of ice and water given out by the county, but they had to =
travel because Poinciana was devastated.  Our fire department's roof was =
torn off by the high force winds completely, with no help there.

The SCHURICK'S themselves never told us how wet with water their own =
house was!!

Mother in law's room wet, son's room wet, their bedroom, living room, =
kitchen wet completely!  The whole house was soaking wet, unlivable!  =
Sad to say, three days later, here came Hurricane Frances, ten times =
longer than Hurricane Charlie which totaled all the walls by means of =
water into every wall of this structure, warping floors, piano, and all =
furniture gone-gone.

All that is left is this:

NOW A FAMILY OF FOUR WITH NO WHERE TO GO !!!!

After they have exhausted their living expenses, their insurance =
company, Sunshine State Insurance refuses to pay the full damages of =
costs to this dwelling even after this family paid their deductibles!  =
The house now smells of mildew and mold, and is noted unsafe.

FEMA can't help or won't.  Although Bill Schurick had open heart =
surgery, he wants to help but can't.  Mary Schurick has heart and back =
problems and their son Louis has medical problems also.

This family is now undergoing treatment for their lungs from mold which =
they inhaled while living in their house for three (3) months post storm =
before they figured out the problem.  With the medical problems I see =
them facing and Sunshine State Insurance Company not setting what must =
be done, I am asking you on their behalf to try to intervene and help =
this family.

They have already gone to mediation as asked by the state to no avail =
and they are in constant contact talking with Lisa Miller and Cheryl =
Jones of Tom Gallagher's office at the Florida Department of Financial =
Services in Tallahassee which is also going nowhere. =20

This insurance company, Sunshine State Insurance, that insured the =
Schurick family house for a number of years, is it not fair to say, that =
the insurance company being Sunshine State Insurance, should pay =
according to the insured policy agreement which was between both =
parties.  This agreement states to bring the damaged house back to it's =
pre-storm condition.

The contractor's that Sunshine State Insurance Company paid for an =
estimate, refused to so the job due to the fact that the SCHURICK'S  =
house can not be repaired at the price Sunshine State Insurance wants to =
pay.  As the FEMA building inspector, Randall reeves has stated in his =
reports that this house needs to be completely renovated.

I hope as our Governor of Florida, you can help this SCHURICK family get =
their home back to the way it was before these three (#) storms hit.

This family of seniors can not afford to hire a lawyer and they make =
just above the income for legal aid.  THEY NEED YOUR HELP.

Miracles happen and I hope to see one for this family,  The SCHURICK'S.

Many thanks,
Doris Ramos
404 Allspice Court
Kissimmee, Florida 34759
Phone number (863) 427-0578
Cell Phone (407) 460-7364

